    {
      "names": [
        "unshare",
        "setns",
        "clone",
        "pivot_root",
        "chroot",
        "sethostname"
      ],
      "action": "SCMP_ACT_ALLOW",
      "comment": "ROOTLESS BUILDER GROUP A. RootlessKit and runc create a nested user+mount+pid+ipc+uts namespace per build step (clone/unshare), enter namespaces (setns), switch the step's root filesystem (pivot_root, chroot fallback) and set the step's hostname. Same filter also applies to tenant code, which is why the kernel's user-namespace rules, hostUsers:false and the absence of CAP_SYS_ADMIN on the outer container are the real gate. Taken from Docker's CAP_SYS_ADMIN/CAP_SYS_CHROOT blocks, made unconditional because a seccomp list cannot see capabilities inside a user namespace."
    },
    {
      "names": [
        "mount",
        "umount",
        "umount2",
        "mount_setattr",
        "move_mount",
        "open_tree",
        "fsopen",
        "fsconfig",
        "fsmount",
        "fspick"
      ],
      "action": "SCMP_ACT_ALLOW",
      "comment": "ROOTLESS BUILDER GROUP B. Mounting the step's /proc, /dev, tmpfs and bind mounts inside the nested mount namespace (classic mount API plus the new fsopen/fsmount API used by runc 1.2+). Seccomp cannot restrict mount by target or by namespace: mounts outside the user namespace are refused by the kernel (needs CAP_SYS_ADMIN in the mount namespace's owning user namespace), and AppArmor rule 'deny mount fstype=...' removes the dangerous filesystems. Dangerous fstypes and 'mount outside the userns' are NOT blocked by this file alone."
    },
